//! [Phase 4, P1.1] E3, the KDA route, in the connector (TC20, oracle part). Generated by
//! impl/harness/phase4/make_p11_tests.py from the harness file below; only the `p11_` test is run.
//! [lifecycle Level 0 connector proof, gate G2-mock part 2] The UNMODIFIED kms-worker at main checks
//! user-decryption requests against the Level 0 ACL **v0.8.0** (account retirement, `retireAccount()`),
//! deployed on a local Anvil node in place of the base ACL v0.7.0.
//!
//! Test-only file. It reuses the baseline real-chain harness (`setup/host.rs`: `AnvilAcl`,
//! `init_host_chains_acl_contracts_anvil`; the repo's `DbInstance::setup_external`) and adds:
//! - the Level 0 ACL implementation, loaded from a forge artifact (`LIFECYCLE_L0_ACL_ARTIFACT`) and
//!   deployed with Zama's own flow (`ERC1967Proxy(EmptyUUPSProxyACL)` then
//!   `upgradeToAndCall(ACL, initializeFromEmptyProxy())`); the exact pre-image (base source at
//!   ed851716c, `LIFECYCLE_BASE_ACL_ARTIFACT`) is deployed the same way as a latency comparator, next to
//!   the baseline's `fhevm_host_bindings` bytecode;
//! - retirement by the real `retireAccount()`: anvil EOAs, local-key EOAs (signed with their own key) or
//!   the dApp contract itself (`DappStub.retireSelf`);
//! - one fresh worker (fresh gateway/KMS mocks) per request, the ACL and the DB persisting across the
//!   requests of a test, so the same request can be sent before and after a retirement;
//! - a NEUTRAL gateway mock: the Coprocessor registry load plus `max_attempts` copies of the gateway tx
//!   (legacy path), so only the connector's own checks can stop a request;
//! - the connector's host-chain URL carries the request label as path, so the JSON-RPC recorder
//!   attributes every ACL call to the request that made it.
//!
//! Paths: legacy gateway-transaction user decryption (direct, delegated) and the RFC-016 unified
//! user decryption (direct entry `owner == user`, delegated entry `owner != user`, on-chain and HTTP
//! sourced).
//!
//! Environment (set by `/srv/lifecycle/scripts/run_level0.sh`):
//! - `LIFECYCLE_ANVIL_URL`, `LIFECYCLE_HOST_RPC_URL`, `LIFECYCLE_HOST_CHAIN_ID`, `LIFECYCLE_SOL_OUT`;
//! - `LIFECYCLE_L0_ACL_ARTIFACT`, `LIFECYCLE_BASE_ACL_ARTIFACT`;
//! - `DATABASE_URL` (+ `PGPASSFILE`): external Postgres, the repo's own `DbInstance::setup_external`.
